ful from both inside and outside. It's considered one of the best mosques in the Shopian district.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Jamia Masjid, Shopian","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7f/Jamia_masjid_shopian.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7f/Jamia_masjid_shopian.jpg","w":1200,"h":675,"author":"Sauood07","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jamia_masjid_shopian.jpg"}},{"id":"srinagar_kathi_darwaza","areaId":"srinagar","name":"Kathi Darwaza","category":"monument","tags":["history","photo"],"location":{"lat":34.10375,"lng":74.82151},"visitMinutes":30,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"srinagar_kathi_darwaza","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":7,"commonsNearby":14,"wikiPageviews":100,"wikidataSitelinks":3,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-21"},"hashtags":["kathidarwaza","srinagar"],"bestLight":"morning","summary":"Kathi Darwaza is a historic gateway located in old city of Srinagar, built in 16th century by Mughal emperor Akbar. Kathi Darwaza along with Sangeen Darwaza serves as gateways to the citadel(Hari Parbat Fort) built on Koh-e-Maran hill.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Kathi Darwaza","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Kathi_Darwaza_01.jpg/1280px-Kathi_Darwaza_01.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Kathi_Darwaza_01.jpg/500px-Kathi_Darwaza_01.jpg","w":1200,"h":800,"author":"Indrajit Das","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathi_Darwaza_01.jpg"}},{"id":"srinagar_salim_ali_national_park","areaId":"srinagar","name":"Salim Ali National Park","category":"park","tags":["nature","photo"],"location":{"lat":34.081,"lng":74.804},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"srinagar_salim_ali_national_park","tickets":[],"signa